  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 29th July 2025, the proposal as shown on the drawing(s) submitted on 29th July 2025 and numbered AD-01-30, AD-01-02, AD-01-00, AD-OS was not lawful within the meanings of Section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990.\r\nThe development fails to comply with the terms of Class A, Clause A.1 (j)(iii) and Class E, Clause E.1(c) of Part 1 of Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended) because the enlarged part of the dwellinghouse would extend beyond a wall forming a side elevation of the original dwellinghouse and would have a width greater than half the width of the original dwellinghouse, and the outbuilding would be situation on land forward of a wall forming the principal elevation of the original dwellinghouse."
